      "content": "but why does the help always feel so forced? like, everyone wants to pull me back into the noise and the struggle, but they don't see the elegance in the stillness. they call it a symptom, but to me, it feels like the only honest moment i've had in years. it feels like a release. don't you think there's something beautiful about a thing reaching its natural, quiet conclusion instead of just dragging on until it's broken?",
